Interpretation
--------------
mean = +0.708 mV : sub-millivolt pre-calibration offset, within typical
                   ADS1263 spec at gain = 1.
RMS  = 1.416 µV  : 35× below the 50 µV target. Lower than the
                   ADS1263_H7_Integration_Notes Test B baseline (~5 µV
                   at 2.5 V VREF), because the bare EVM doesn't include
                   the legacy Waveshare HAT's 4.4× input attenuator.
                   Consistent with the chip's intrinsic noise spec at
                   400 SPS, PGA bypass.
RMS ≠ 0          : Conversions advance sample-to-sample. SPI / RDATA1 /
                   START1 path is healthy (the stuck-read guard in cp5
                   did not trip).


Issues encountered and resolved during this bring-up
----------------------------------------------------
1. BUILD FAILURE — 'PWM_0' was not declared in this scope.
   The Arduino-mbed Portenta H7 core packaged with PlatformIO
   (`platform = ststm32`, `board = portenta_h7_m7`) does NOT define
   PWM_0/1/2; only the high-numbered PWM_8/PWM_9 are exposed as
   macros. Fixed by switching to STM32 pin names directly:
     PWM_0  →  PA_8   (J15-25, /CS)
     PWM_1  →  PC_6   (J15-27, /DRDY)
     PWM_2  →  PC_7   (J15-29, /RESET)
   Mapping confirmed against doc/PortentaH7_ABX00042_Pinout.pdf
   page 12 (J2_odd table) and doc/PortentaMidCarrier_ASX00055_Pinout.pdf
   page 3 (J15 table).

2. FIRST PASS, BAD NOISE-FLOOR INTERPRETATION — cp5 reported
   mean = +2500.000 mV, RMS = 0.000 µV. The threshold check passed
   but the reading was meaningless: cp5 was configured with
   INPMUX=0x01 (AIN0/AIN1) and REFMUX=0x00 (internal 2.5 V), but
   on this rig AIN0/AIN1 carry the external 5 V reference voltage.
   So the diagnostic was measuring the reference voltage with the
   internal 2.5 V reference, saturating positive full-scale with no
   noise expression.
   Fixed by reconfiguring cp5 for the rig's actual setup:
     REFMUX = 0x09       (external ref via AIN0+ / AIN1-)
     INPMUX = 0xAA       (AINCOM-shorted — true Vshort noise test)
     VREF   = 5.0 V      (in the volts-per-code math)
   Also added a new RMS == 0.0 stuck-read guard so this failure
   mode would fail-fast next time instead of silently passing.
